# Canonical Data Mapping

## 1. Purpose

This document defines how the original Budget vs Actual Variance Navigator dataset is transformed into the Phase 3 canonical data structure.

The canonical source of truth will be:

`data/canonical/intelligence_data.csv`

## 2. Source Dataset

- **Source file:** `data/source-sample/source_sample.csv`
- **Original records:** 18
- **Original columns:** 8
- **Canonical columns:** 20
- **Financial measures:** 4
- **Expected canonical records:** 72

Each source row generates four canonical records, one for each financial measure.

## 3. Canonical Column Mapping

| Canonical column | Source or transformation | Mapping rule |
|---|---|---|
| `record_id` | Generated | Unique deterministic ID for each canonical record |
| `record_type` | Generated | `financial_metric` |
| `observed_at` | `month` | Convert month to ISO 8601 UTC, using the first day of the month |
| `entity_id` | `cost_centre` | Preserve cost centre identifier |
| `related_entity_id` | Not available | Leave blank |
| `entity_name` | `department` | Preserve department name associated with the cost centre |
| `category` | `account_category` | Preserve account category |
| `subcategory` | Not available | Leave blank |
| `status` | Not available | Leave blank |
| `stage` | Not available | Leave blank |
| `metric_name` | Financial measure | Use `budget_amount`, `actual_amount`, `committed_amount`, or `forecast_amount` |
| `metric_value` | Financial measure | Preserve the corresponding numeric amount |
| `metric_unit` | Generated | `USD` |
| `text_value` | Not applicable | Leave blank |
| `latitude` | Not available | Leave blank |
| `longitude` | Not available | Leave blank |
| `source_name` | Generated | `backend/budget_data.csv` |
| `source_record_id` | Generated | Stable source-row identifier |
| `is_synthetic` | Generated | `true` |
| `data_version` | Generated | `1.0.0` |

## 4. Financial Measure Expansion

Each original source record is expanded into four canonical records.

| Original source field | Canonical metric_name | Canonical metric_value |
|---|---|---|
| `budget_amount` | `budget_amount` | Original budget value |
| `actual_amount` | `actual_amount` | Original actual value |
| `committed_amount` | `committed_amount` | Original committed value |
| `forecast_amount` | `forecast_amount` | Original forecast value |

For example, the first source row generates four records for:

- Cost centre: CC-101
- Department: Engineering
- Category: Cloud Infrastructure
- Reporting month: January 2026

The four records preserve the original values of 45000, 48000, 2000, and 50000 respectively.

## 5. Identifier Strategy

- `record_id` will be generated uniquely and deterministically.
- `source_record_id` will identify the original source CSV row.
- All four canonical records generated from one source row will share the same `source_record_id`.
- The identifiers will remain stable across repeated pipeline runs using the same source data.

## 6. Date Standardization

The original month values use the format `Mon YYYY`.

They will be converted to the first day of the corresponding month in ISO 8601 UTC format.

Examples:

- `Jan 2026` → `2026-01-01T00:00:00Z`
- `Feb 2026` → `2026-02-01T00:00:00Z`
- `Mar 2026` → `2026-03-01T00:00:00Z`

This represents the reporting month, not an exact transaction timestamp.

## 7. Numeric and Missing Value Rules

- Financial amounts will remain numeric.
- Currency symbols and thousands separators will not be added.
- The currency unit will be represented by `USD`.
- Unavailable source fields will remain blank.
- No unsupported values will be invented.
- Boolean values will use `true` and `false`.

## 8. Expected Output

The canonical dataset is expected to contain:

- 72 records.
- Exactly 20 columns.
- All 18 original source records represented.
- Four financial measures for each source record.
- Unique canonical record identifiers.
- Preserved source-row relationships.

## 9. Preservation and Traceability

The original source dataset remains unchanged.

The canonical dataset will be reproducible from the preserved source snapshot using the Phase 3 data pipeline.

The `source_name` and `source_record_id` fields provide traceability back to the original source.

## 10. Conclusion

The mapping converts the original eight-column financial dataset into the required 20-column canonical structure.

All available financial measures and source relationships are preserved without introducing unsupported business information.
</file>

